{title: 044 - Morning Has Broken}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #044 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 44}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Morning [G]has [Am]bro[Dm]ken [G]Like the first [F]morn[G]ing,
[Am]Blackbird has [G7]spo[Dm]ken [C]Like the first [Gsus]bird.[G]
[C]Praise for [G]the [Am]sing[Dm]ing! [C]Praise for the [Am]morn[D7]ing!
[G]Praise for them [C]spring[Am]ing [F]Fresh from [G]the [C]Word!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Sweet [G]the [Am]rain's [Dm]new [G]fall [F]sunlit [G]from heaven,
[Am]Like [G7]the [Dm]first dewfall [C]on [Gsus]the [G]first grass.
[C]Praise [G]for [Am]the [Dm]sweetness [C]of [Am]the [D7]wet garden,
[G]Sprung [C]in [Am]completeness [F]where [G]His [C]feet pass.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Mine [G]is [Am]the [Dm]sunlight! [G]Mine [F]is [G]the morning
[Am]Born [G7]of [Dm]the one [C]light [Gsus]Eden [G]saw play!
[C][G]Praise [Am]with [Dm]elation, [C]Praise [Am]every [D7]morning,
[G]God's [C]recreation [Am]of [F]the [G]new [C]day!
{end_of_verse}
